          88
        ]
      },
      "finding": "Each output has its own lifecycle and XID. The Gst downstream queue is one leaky buffer; appsrc is additionally bounded at one BGR frame; the four-entry frames map retains metadata references rather than image layers. Raw publication uses a complete private temp frame and os.replace; RawFrameReader reads one inode/version, suppresses duplicates and rejects rollback/stale frames. New Gst buffers contain complete immutable BGR bytes. Nothing in this reviewed transport accumulates old face drawings or GTK Pixbuf frames."
    },
